Consider a Diophantine equation system over the positive integers:
\[ \left\{
\begin{array}{rcl}
\frac{y+3}{3x} & \leq & 4 \\
y & \leq & 3z + x + 7
\end{array}
\right.
\]
and suppose that \( y = 5z - 1 \). Determine all positive integer solutions \((x, y, z)\) satisfying these constraints. Count the total number of such solutions.

